  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Ammonia is consered a strong ligand generally, but in reality, strength of a ligand depends on the metal it is interacting with. As it stands, NH<sub>3</sub>&nbsp;isn't a strong enough ligand to cause pairing up in Ni, hence the magnetic moment remains the same.<br /><br /><math><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"><mrow><mtext>Ni</mtext> <msub> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>6</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mo>+</mo> </mrow> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>6</mn> <msub> <mtext>NH</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mo>→</mo> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>Ni</mtext> <msub> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>NH</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>6</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mo>+</mo> </mrow> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>6</mn> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>sp</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msup> <msup> <mtext>d</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>Hybridisation</mo> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>sp</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msup> <msup> <mtext>d</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>Hybridisation</mo> </mrow> </math><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>μ</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>2.8 BM</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>μ</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>2.8 BM</mo> </mrow> </math>",
